NAME
    sort - sort lines

SYNOPSIS
    sort [-n] [-r]

DESCRIPTION
    Sorts piped stdin (or trailing literal text) by line - ordinal string
    comparison by default, numeric with -n, reversed with -r. No -u (that's
    'uniq's job - pair them, 'sort | uniq', the way real shell usage does
    before reaching for 'sort -u' as a shortcut), no field/key selection, no
    locale-aware collation.

EXAMPLES
    watch list | sort -n
